---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<Layout title="Home">
  <div class="hero">
    <video class="hero-video" autoplay muted loop playsinline>
      <source src={`${base}videos/backgrounds/home.mp4`} type="video/mp4" />
    </video>
    <img src={`${base}logo_tourney_balance.png`} alt="Tourney Balance" class="hero-logo" />
  </div>

  <div class="page-body">
    <div class="page-body-inner">
      <h1>Welcome to Tourney Balance</h1>
      <p>
        Tourney Balance is a balance mod for high difficulty modded gameplay
        for Warhammer: Vermintide 2. This site documents the mod's patch
        history and how its balance changes differ from official.
      </p>

      <h2>What is Tourney Balance</h2>
      <p>
        Tourney Balance aims to rebalance many classes and weapons by
        nerfing overperformers and buffing weaker or lesser used options,
        improving variety and choice for players. Despite numerous
        adjustments to numbers and values, the goal is to stay as close to
        the feel of official game balance as possible, so that play styles
        and the original design intent are retained.
      </p>
      <p>
        Tourney Balance (TB) mostly focuses on balancing around the
        Cataclysm 3 Deathwish Onslaught (C3DWONS) difficulty and its higher
        difficulty versions, such as C3DWONS+ and C3DW Dutch Spice. The
        original intention of Tourney Balance is to serve as the baseline
        for the various tourneys held in the modded scene, such as the
        Onslaught Series.
      </p>
      <p>
        The full documentation of all the mod's changes can be found <a href={`${base}changes/`}>here</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Features</h2>
      <p>
        Alongside its balance changes, the mod also includes several tools
        used for events and basic quality-of-life improvements:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Mod Checker</strong> — displays any banned tournament mods currently used by you or your team.</li>
        <li><strong>Disable Bots</strong> — disables bots and removes their portraits.</li>
        <li><strong>Pause</strong> — pauses the game.</li>
        <li><strong>Restart</strong> — restarts the current game.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Credits</h2>
      <p>
        Thanks to the Tourney Balance Team, and the continued support and
        feedback from many different community members, the mod is still
        receiving updates.
      </p>

      <h2>Community</h2>
      <p>
        If you would also like to join the modded scene — be it for tourneys, regular games, or just discussions about the mods in
        question — feel free to join the <a href="https://discord.gg/MS4vWSQrEh">Onslaught Series</a> and <a href="https://discord.gg/hyeADkwp">VT Modded Community</a> Discord servers!
      </p>
      <p>
        The source code for the mod can be found <a href="https://github.com/Camilo-Guzman/Tourney-Balance">here</a>.
      </p>

      <p>
        <a href={`${base}patch-notes/`}>Read the Patch Notes →</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .hero {
    position: relative;
    height: 100vh;
  }

  .hero-video {
    position: fixed;
    top: 0;
    left: 0;
    width: 100vw;
    height: 100vh;
    object-fit: cover;
    z-index: -1;
  }

  .hero-logo {
    position: absolute;
    top: 50%;
    left: 50%;
    transform: translate(-50%, -50%);
    max-width: min(50vw, 480px);
    height: auto;
  }

  .page-body {
    position: relative;
    background: var(--color-bg);
    /* Break out of Layout.astro's <main> max-width/centering so the
       background spans the full viewport width, regardless of how narrow
       or wide main's own content column is. */
    width: 100vw;
    margin-left: calc(50% - 50vw);
    margin-right: calc(50% - 50vw);
  }

  .page-body-inner {
    max-width: 1100px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 2rem;
  }
</style>
